From 0d53383d5d8d9ef0c9adb66a0e151afa3b7105ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:19:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [DVBridge] Bring the link up from scratch on a dual-mode
 DisplayPort connector of nvidia-drm

Through the HDMI port of an HP ZBook 17 G6 (Quadro RTX 4000), which nvidia-drm names DP-2 and
drives as HDMI through the TMDS output of its dual-mode DisplayPort port (NV_DUAL_MODE_TMDS 1),
native Dolby Vision started "at a lottery" after a change of the refresh rate (2 to 12 tries), and
with the GUI at another rate than the video the TV showed pink and purple: the tunnel read as RGB,
while the DRM state had the mode of the video and its flips came at its rate (issue #4). That
breaks fail closed. Native output entered there in the commit of the change of mode (held for its
first frame: CModeChangeHold, START; or moved into from the video before: CDVModeMove), on a
running head; leaving it, nvidia-drm turns the head off and on. Through a USB-C to HDMI adapter
of the same laptop the change of rate worked. Why the TV does not take the transport on that port
is not known.

On a connector whose link native output brings up from scratch, NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE::
LinkFromScratch() (a DisplayPort connector of nvidia-drm driven as HDMI now), the order is now the
one of the exit path:
 - the mode goes out alone first: a change of mode for a native Dolby Vision video is not held for
   its first frame (CModeChangeHold::StartHolds()), and native output does not move into the mode
   of the next video (CDVModeMove::Moves()): it ends, the mode goes out, and it enters again;
 - the transport enters only in the mode on the output (CDRMAtomic::IsSelectedModeCommitted(), from
   CCommittedMode: the mode that an accepted modeset carried, not a modeset pending, and not the one
   of a commit that fell back to the request before it). Otherwise nothing is committed and the
   frame is not shown: two seconds of them end native output for the video, which goes on in the
   ordinary output, and the TV keeps the picture it has meanwhile;
 - in that mode the transport enters with the head turned off and on, as it leaves: NVKMS brings
   the head and the link up from scratch with the Dolby InfoFrame from their first frame. Once per
   capture; a refusal of it leaves the frames after it to the entry in place, as on HDMI. Not while
   the display is meant to be off (DPMS).

kodi.log says which: "native Dolby Vision entered with the output turned off and on again on
connector DP-2, which brings its link up from scratch", or that it waits for the mode, or that
turning the output off or on was refused.

An HDMI connector is not one (the RTX 4080 SUPER with the LG C5 takes the mode and the transport in
one commit), nor is a connector of the kernel backends: nothing changes for them. The host test
prints every decision of StartHolds(), DVRestoreJoins(), StopHolds() and Moves() without the new
field (1537 of them) and they are the same with the headers before and after; the end of native
output in one commit with the next mode is not touched.

Host test: dualmode_test, 22 checks; with the headers before, 5 of them fail. Whether this ends the
lottery and the pink can only be seen on that laptop and its TV.
