+
+/*!
+ * Hades: whether native Dolby Vision brings the link of the connector up from scratch: a dual-mode
+ * DisplayPort connector that the card drives as HDMI now (DrivenAsHdmi() for "DP"). Through the
+ * HDMI port of the HP ZBook 17 G6 (DP-2, issue #4) native output started "at a lottery" after a
+ * change of the refresh rate (2 to 12 tries), and with the GUI at another rate than the video the
+ * TV showed pink and purple: the tunnel read as RGB, while the DRM state had the mode of the video
+ * and its flips came at that rate. Native output started there in the commit of the change of mode
+ * (CModeChangeHold, CDVModeMove), and on a running head; leaving it, nvidia-drm turns the head off
+ * and on. Through a USB-C to HDMI adapter of the same laptop the change of rate worked. Why the TV
+ * does not take the transport there is not known; on such a connector the mode now goes out alone
+ * first, and native output enters with the head turned off and on, as it leaves. An HDMI connector
+ * is not one: an RTX 4080 SUPER with an LG C5 takes the mode and the transport in one commit.
+ */
+inline bool LinkFromScratch(std::string_view type, std::optional<uint64_t> dualModeTmds)
+{
